title: isomorphic git with memfs
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

This notebook creates a Git repository entirely in browser memory. It uses [[isomorphic-git|https://isomorphic-git.org/]] with [[memfs|https://github.com/streamich/memfs]] rather than LightningFS: `memfs` supplies the Node-compatible `fs` API isomorphic-git expects, while a new volume makes every run isolated and disposable.

The setup cells initialize the repository, create and stage two files, and make an initial commit. Then use the buttons to create an untracked random file, append a line to the tracked `notebook-files/notes.txt`, or stage and commit all working-tree changes. No repository is cloned and no remote is contacted.

`memfs` file events provide the reactive value that drives the live filesystem and status displays below. The watcher is restricted to `notebook-files/`, avoiding a feedback loop from isomorphic-git's `.git` writes. The filesystem display shows the current `volume.toJSON()` value, the status display distinguishes the untracked random files from the modified notes file, and the commit-history display uses isomorphic-git's `git.log()` API.

